blurb: The South Portland School Board discussed the challenging FY27 budget, driven
  by declining enrollment and depleted fund balances, and provided guidance to the
  administration to prepare a budget with a tax increase target between 3.1% and 9.7%.
  Key ideas for cost savings, including elementary school reconfiguration and a single
  middle school start time, were debated amidst concerns for taxpayer burden and student
  impact.
